entries.content:
revv
Reverse a whole pattern. See also `rev` for reversing each cycle.
Example:
// This is the same as `<[g e] [d c]>`. If `rev()` is used, you get
// the same as `<[d c] [g e]>`, where each cycle reverses, but the order of
// cycles stays the same.
note("<[c d] [e g]>").revv()

